{"title":"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Recursion)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Recursion)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Euclid_Spark_(ANIMATED_SHORT)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Euclid Spark (ANIMATED SHORT)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The land of Catania uses gold coins and silver coins. Gold coins are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mm thick and silver coins are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mm thick. In how many ways can Taylor make a stack of coins that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mm tall using any arrangement of gold and silver coins, assuming order matters?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b8355a7893a6c923024f72d27acf76691a87516f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }3\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }7\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }10\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }13\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"382\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A stack containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or more silver coins is at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mm tall, so a stack of height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mm may contain at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> silver coins. We now use casework on the number of silver coins:\n</p>\n<ul><li>An <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mm stack with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> silver coins contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> gold coins.  There is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/c/c3c60ac26253c3049c56211312b9314d23a83709.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{8}{0} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"72\" height=\"55\" /> such stack.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>An <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mm stack with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> silver coin contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> gold coins.  There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/1/3617ca164aac4e358010b5dcec888082cb1c2cd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{6}{1} = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"72\" height=\"55\" /> such stacks.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>An <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mm stack with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> silver coins contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> gold coins.  There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/0/f401413a5807bd29f485f438f9b97173ecd58351.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{4}{2} = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"70\" height=\"53\" /> such stacks.</li></ul>\n<p>Thus, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/7/7d7a5c874196e1366ea4a7186e9b2d9ab570fd34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+6+6=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"162\" height=\"30\" /> different <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mm stacks.  \n</p><p>~Baihly2024, Pinotation, Pillowwillowtree01, edited by j314andrews, edited by kirigami789\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Recursion.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Recursion)\">Solution 2 (Recursion)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Recursion)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/bea4d576937a04ec200b1037fc8ee33e8f744cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of different stacks of height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> mm.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b1171ce641826e9aca894162f9c15a57f6b46e09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />, as the only possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mm stack is a single gold coin.  Also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/8/bd8754c11b59d41eef1ce5d0e1f2952797e07ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />, as the only possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mm stack is two gold coins, while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/9/b79cb19dd1156bd44cdfeb4bfe6c60b43b591c48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, as the two possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mm stacks are either three gold coins or one silver coin.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/e/c1ef767dfc3df471239be2977a059086b929f922.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\geq 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, a stack of height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> mm can be formed by placing a stack of height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/e/8ee38a85837f9209748be5df945d770fdfdb036e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> mm on a gold coin or placing a stack of height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/9/e096f97a981ce280055471c6f832d7e4effc817e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k - 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> mm on a silver coin.  Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93fba67899125f5f5963a9c8313b6a4579db5d29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k = a_{k-1} + a_{k-3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"16\" />.  So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/5/ef5369e3ee673c608c5dc68036843aff1d4298db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/a/b3ac403fc200e3767f6516fb602718e78cbbb41b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_5 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/9/90981fe0219a82e27d2f1cd05fd1eb0d3a0ba8a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_6 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/8/2381951d5766f743e130663afe0005e2e2e1e7f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_7 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/787d7460d7a91ccf9889a93db176f02f3586b61f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_8 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"108\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>-j314andrews\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gzXlOkLl24U\">https://youtu.be/gzXlOkLl24U</a>\n</p><p>~TheSmartGreekMathDude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_DDM\">Video Solution by DDM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by DDM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/nY1hhVbEeBk\">https://youtu.be/nY1hhVbEeBk</a>\n</p><p>~piggydude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Thinking Feet\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/05dW8HbwXRA\">https://youtu.be/05dW8HbwXRA</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Euclid_Spark_.28ANIMATED_SHORT.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Euclid_Spark_(ANIMATED_SHORT)\">Video Solution by Euclid Spark (ANIMATED SHORT)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Euclid Spark (ANIMATED SHORT)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/wi82LwFgtv8\">https://www.youtube.com/shorts/wi82LwFgtv8</a>\n</p><p>~MathRules2022\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YJnsl4zjdK8\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YJnsl4zjdK8</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action